{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "8226908",
      "title": "Using Effect Cleanup Functions & Using Keys for Resetting Components",
      "sourceHash": "abf0c08ed742c0f37ddf51edeeb98d76c734f5c90dad3a8b949e32521b1325f1",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.33,
          "end": 3.57,
          "en": "Now, where's this strange behavior",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.57,
          "end": 7.587,
          "en": "coming from that this progress bar is empty,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.587,
          "end": 10.83,
          "en": "but we only move on to the next question",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.83,
          "end": 12.933,
          "en": "after a couple of extra seconds?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.86,
          "end": 15.39,
          "en": "Well, the problem is simply",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.39,
          "end": 19.11,
          "en": "that the progress bar is depleting too quickly.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.11,
          "end": 21.42,
          "en": "We have a ten second timer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.42,
          "end": 23.25,
          "en": "but if you set a stopwatch,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.25,
          "end": 25.95,
          "en": "you'll see that the progress bar is empty",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 25.95,
          "end": 28.35,
          "en": "after five seconds.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 28.35,
          "end": 32.34,
          "en": "And that's happening because this interval here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.34,
          "end": 35.46,
          "en": "is actually getting triggered twice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 35.46,
          "end": 38.61,
          "en": "and therefore we have two intervals running",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 38.61,
          "end": 42.27,
          "en": "behind the scenes that keep on updating this state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 42.27,
          "end": 46.77,
          "en": "And therefore the progress bar is empty in half the time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 46.77,
          "end": 47.603,
          "en": "You can see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 47.603,
          "end": 51.9,
          "en": "that it's getting triggered twice here in the console.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 51.9,
          "end": 55.17,
          "en": "And that's happening as I mentioned before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 55.17,
          "end": 60.17,
          "en": "because we have React's StrictMode turned on in main JSX.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 62.01,
          "end": 65.19,
          "en": "Now during development, and only there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 65.19,
          "end": 68.58,
          "en": "this StrictMode will actually execute",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 68.58,
          "end": 71.1,
          "en": "every component function twice,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 71.1,
          "end": 76.1,
          "en": "which is done to help you catch certain errors in your app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 76.26,
          "end": 77.91,
          "en": "Because in theory,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 77.91,
          "end": 81.51,
          "en": "your app should work in exactly the same way,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 81.51,
          "end": 85.53,
          "en": "no matter if a component function gets executed once",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 85.53,
          "end": 89.94,
          "en": "when being rendered to the screen or 100 times.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 89.94,
          "end": 92.52000000000001,
          "en": "And clearly here, that's not the case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 92.52000000000001,
          "end": 96.87,
          "en": "which is an indicator for a bug we have in our code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 96.87,
          "end": 98.91,
          "en": "So here in this case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 98.91,
          "end": 103.68,
          "en": "StrictMode helps us identify that we have a bug.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 103.68,
          "end": 105.72,
          "en": "But what is the problem?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 105.72,
          "end": 110.55,
          "en": "Well, the problem here is that when this effect function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 110.55,
          "end": 112.56,
          "en": "gets executed twice here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 112.56,
          "end": 115.59,
          "en": "we have two running intervals.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 115.59,
          "end": 117.27000000000001,
          "en": "That should not be the case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 117.27000000000001,
          "end": 122.27,
          "en": "And what's missing here in our code is a cleanup function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 122.34,
          "end": 125.73,
          "en": "We have to clean up the existing interval",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 125.73,
          "end": 128.64,
          "en": "if this effect function runs again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 128.64,
          "end": 130.35,
          "en": "And if we do that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 130.35,
          "end": 132.69,
          "en": "it wouldn't matter if this effect function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 132.69,
          "end": 134.64,
          "en": "gets called 10 times,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 134.64,
          "end": 138.42000000000002,
          "en": "because if we always clean up the old intervals,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 138.42000000000002,
          "end": 141.32999999999998,
          "en": "we'll only have one interval up and running",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 141.32999999999998,
          "end": 142.503,
          "en": "at the same time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 143.88,
          "end": 146.31,
          "en": "And this is something we should add anyways,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 146.31,
          "end": 149.49,
          "en": "because at the moment if I move to a different question",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 149.49,
          "end": 154.07999999999998,
          "en": "we also have the problem that the old timer keeps on running",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 154.07999999999998,
          "end": 156.69,
          "en": "and is not being reset.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 156.69,
          "end": 159.57,
          "en": "And that should eventually also change",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 159.57,
          "end": 161.88,
          "en": "and therefore will also need a cleanup function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 161.88,
          "end": 163.56,
          "en": "for that reason.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 163.56,
          "end": 167.7,
          "en": "So let's go here to the question timer component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 167.7,
          "end": 172.38,
          "en": "and store a reference to that interval in a constant",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 172.38,
          "end": 175.02,
          "en": "and then add that cleanup function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 175.02,
          "end": 178.26,
          "en": "as you learned it as a return value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 178.26,
          "end": 179.913,
          "en": "in that effect function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 180.84,
          "end": 182.79,
          "en": "And this cleanup function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 182.79,
          "end": 186.51,
          "en": "will then automatically be executed by React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 186.51,
          "end": 189.54,
          "en": "before it runs this effect function again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 189.54,
          "end": 193.41,
          "en": "or when this component is unmounted from the DOM.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 193.41,
          "end": 195.783,
          "en": "So if it disappears from the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 198.21,
          "end": 200.28,
          "en": "So therefore here in this cleanup function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 200.28,
          "end": 202.68,
          "en": "we now should call clear interval",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 202.68,
          "end": 205.173,
          "en": "and pass this interval reference to it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 206.64,
          "end": 209.49,
          "en": "And we should actually do the same for the timer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 209.49,
          "end": 213.69,
          "en": "because otherwise this timer will keep on going.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 213.69,
          "end": 214.74,
          "en": "And for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 214.74,
          "end": 217.95,
          "en": "if this component would be removed from this screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 217.95,
          "end": 222.9,
          "en": "because we reach that game over screen here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 222.9,
          "end": 225.453,
          "en": "we of course wanna clean up the timer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 226.35,
          "end": 229.44,
          "en": "So therefore here we should also store a reference",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 229.44,
          "end": 232.74,
          "en": "to that timer in a variable or constant.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 232.74,
          "end": 235.92000000000002,
          "en": "And then add that cleanup function here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 235.92000000000002,
          "end": 240.003,
          "en": "where we clear that timeout by passing the timer to it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 241.71,
          "end": 242.94,
          "en": "And now with that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 242.94,
          "end": 245.49,
          "en": "with those cleanup functions added,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 245.49,
          "end": 247.17,
          "en": "if we now reload",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 247.17,
          "end": 249.99,
          "en": "we will see that this progress bar",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 249.99,
          "end": 253.05,
          "en": "does not deplete that quickly anymore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 253.05,
          "end": 255.3,
          "en": "but instead works as intended.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 255.3,
          "end": 257.01,
          "en": "And therefore, once it's empty,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 257.01,
          "end": 259.56,
          "en": "we move on to the next question.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 259.56,
          "end": 261.69,
          "en": "But of course, now we have the problem",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 261.69,
          "end": 266.69,
          "en": "that the timer and this progress bar is never reset.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 266.76,
          "end": 271.76,
          "en": "Now why is that timer and progress bar not reset",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 271.8,
          "end": 274.023,
          "en": "when we move on to a new question?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 275.4,
          "end": 278.64,
          "en": "Well, because this question timer component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 278.64,
          "end": 281.31,
          "en": "doesn't get recreated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 281.31,
          "end": 282.21,
          "en": "Keep in mind",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 282.21,
          "end": 285.39,
          "en": "that we're using the question timer component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 285.39,
          "end": 288.6,
          "en": "in the quiz component here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 288.6,
          "end": 291.84000000000003,
          "en": "And when we move on to a new question,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 291.84000000000003,
          "end": 295.32,
          "en": "we do that by storing a user answer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 295.32,
          "end": 298.26,
          "en": "And then the act of question index changes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 298.26,
          "end": 300.843,
          "en": "because the length of user answers changed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 301.83,
          "end": 306.83,
          "en": "But therefore, of course this JSX code just gets updated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 307.05,
          "end": 311.67,
          "en": "But this question timer component is not being recreated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 311.67,
          "end": 313.38,
          "en": "because it hasn't changed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 313.38,
          "end": 315.96,
          "en": "It was part of the DOM before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 315.96,
          "end": 319.05,
          "en": "It is still part of the DOM now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 319.05,
          "end": 321.09,
          "en": "The only thing that changed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 321.09,
          "end": 324.12,
          "en": "is the question text that's being displayed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 324.12,
          "end": 326.613,
          "en": "and the answers that are displayed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 327.6,
          "end": 330.93,
          "en": "But this component was there and is there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 330.93,
          "end": 334.77,
          "en": "and therefore it's not unmounted, not remounted,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 334.77,
          "end": 338.37,
          "en": "and therefore the timers and intervals in that component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 338.37,
          "end": 340.17,
          "en": "are not reset.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 340.17,
          "end": 342.9,
          "en": "Now of course here in this application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 342.9,
          "end": 346.8,
          "en": "we'd like to have this timer to be reset though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 346.8,
          "end": 350.223,
          "en": "because of course it should reset when the question changed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 351.18,
          "end": 354.87,
          "en": "And there is a simple yet very powerful trick",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 354.87,
          "end": 358.11,
          "en": "you can use in React to achieve this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 358.11,
          "end": 361.8,
          "en": "You can add a key to this component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 361.8,
          "end": 365.1,
          "en": "because this key prop can actually be added",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 365.1,
          "end": 368.37,
          "en": "to any element and any component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 368.37,
          "end": 373.17,
          "en": "because key is a built-in prop React is looking for.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 373.17,
          "end": 376.41,
          "en": "And you already learned that you should use this key",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 376.41,
          "end": 378.48,
          "en": "when outputting list data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 378.48,
          "end": 381.48,
          "en": "because there this key helps React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 381.48,
          "end": 384.3,
          "en": "identify those different list items",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 384.3,
          "end": 387.87,
          "en": "and it helps React manage that list efficiently",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 387.87,
          "end": 389.913,
          "en": "behind the scenes, so to say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 391.62,
          "end": 395.55,
          "en": "But the key prop also has another purpose.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 395.55,
          "end": 398.90999999999997,
          "en": "Whenever it changes on a component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 398.90999999999997,
          "end": 402.18,
          "en": "even if that component is not part of a list,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 402.18,
          "end": 404.01,
          "en": "whenever it changes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 404.01,
          "end": 408.39,
          "en": "React will destroy the old component instance",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 408.39,
          "end": 409.83299999999997,
          "en": "and create a new one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 410.76,
          "end": 414.57,
          "en": "So it will unmount and remount it basically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 414.57,
          "end": 416.94,
          "en": "And that's exactly what we need here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 416.94,
          "end": 420.9,
          "en": "because I wanna recreate this question timer component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 420.9,
          "end": 423.303,
          "en": "whenever we switch to a new question.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 424.5,
          "end": 428.49,
          "en": "And therefore we could set the question timer key here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 428.49,
          "end": 431.28,
          "en": "to the act of question index,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 136,
          "start": 431.28,
          "end": 434.373,
          "en": "which will change whenever the question changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
